<section class="what-is section-pad" aria-labelledby="what-is-heading">
  <div class="container-wide">
    <div class="what-is-inner animate-in" style="--delay: 100ms">
      <p class="text-eyebrow">What is Cinch?</p>
      <h2 id="what-is-heading" class="what-is-headline">
        An open-source remote clipboard for developers.
      </h2>
      <p class="what-is-lead">
        Cinch is a Unix-native CLI that pipes terminal output from any machine
        straight to your local clipboard. Run <code>cinch push</code> on a
        remote host, <code>cinch pull</code> on your laptop, and the bytes are
        there — over SSH, inside tmux, from a Docker container, or from CI.
        Every clip is end-to-end encrypted with AES-256-GCM before it leaves
        the device, so the relay only ever stores ciphertext. Use the hosted
        relay at <code>api.cinchcli.com</code> or self-host a single Go binary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .what-is {
    /* Tighter than full section-pad so it reads as a continuation of the hero */
    padding-top: 4rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .what-is-inner {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .what-is-headline {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--text-1);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .what-is-lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1.6vw, 1.1875rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-2);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .what-is-lead code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--text-1);
    background: var(--bg-card-2);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .what-is {
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
      padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
